      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1878, La Motte boasted two general stores, a Methodist church built in 1853, a Masonic lodge, and a carriage factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/la_motte_iowa",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Harris Wagon and Carriage Shop, built in 1871, shifted from horse‑drawn vehicles to a harness shop, then a hardware store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/la_motte_iowa",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A narrow‑gauge rail line opened in 1846, linking La Motte to Dubuque and Davenport, and a depot built in 1879 boosted trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Motte%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Chicago, Milwaukee & St. Paul Narrow Gauge Depot in La Motte is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
